<title>EGYPT: Egypt to increase area planted with cotton.</title>
<headline>Egypt to increase area planted with cotton.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-01-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt will increase the area to be planted with cotton by 100,000 acres (40,000 hectares) to one million acres in the next season, starting in February, a newspaper said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The area is forecast to produce 400,000 tonnes of cotton, the government daily al-Ahram said. The country produced around 360,000 tonnes last season.</p>
<p>Egypt had said it expects to export between 125,000 and 150,000 tonnes of this year's harvest. After 18 weeks of the marketing season, it has exported 62,073 tonnes.</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom+ 20 2 578 3290/1</p>
